<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The Silati mark, inverted from public/silati-icon.svg in the web repo.

  That file is a solid tile whose LOGO IS THE HOLES, which an adaptive icon cannot use: the
  launcher masks the layer to a circle/squircle, so a full-bleed tile would clip the mark's
  edges. Inverting it here costs one trick instead of a redrawn asset - a full-canvas
  rectangle is prepended to the original path data and the whole thing is filled evenOdd, so
  every region covered twice (the tile body) drops out and the holes (the mark, and the
  details drawn inside it) are what remains.

  Generated from the source SVG, not typed. Re-run the same transform if the mark changes.
  The 0.9 scale sizes the mark to the 72dp safe zone; nudge it if the icon reads too big or
  too small on a real launcher.
-->
